// Project descriptions and photo counts, taken from the original project pages.
window.BEPLAN_DETAILS = {"optident-wisniowy-business-park-warsaw":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The project involved the creation of a modern, multifunctional space combining a dental equipment exhibition and demonstration area, meeting spaces, and a dedicated training room for professional education and workshops."},{"type":"p","text":"Despite its relatively small size, the project required careful coordination and execution of multiple construction and technical disciplines to ensure functionality, flexibility and a consistent interior finish."},{"type":"p","text":"Our scope of works included: 🔹 General construction and fit-out works 🔹 Electrical installations and lighting 🔹 IT infrastructure and data installations 🔹 Ventilation works and technical coordination 🔹 Finishing works and final handover"}],"photos":6},"carl-zeiss-center-lljubljana-slovenia":{"blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"CARL ZEISS | LJUBLJANA, SLOVENIA"},{"type":"p","text":"Corporate Office | Design &amp; Build"},{"type":"p","text":"BEPLAN Design + Build delivered the new Carl Zeiss corporate offices in Ljubljana, Slovenia, creating a modern, functional workplace aligned with ZEISS global corporate standards."},{"type":"p","text":"The project involved architectural and interior design, technical coordination, and fit-out works, with a focus on optimising space efficiency, employee comfort, and workplace functionality."},{"type":"p","text":"The new office combines collaborative workspaces, meeting rooms, and supporting facilities, integrating contemporary finishes, architectural lighting, and carefully selected materials to reflect the ZEISS corporate identity."},{"type":"p","text":"The result is a welcoming, efficient, and professional working environment that supports collaboration and the company’s international workplace strategy."}],"photos":6},"nestle-coffee-degustation-warsaw":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Nestlé Coffee Degustation is a dedicated tasting and presentation space designed to welcome clients and showcase the coffee experience in a warm, elegant, and functional environment. The project combines contemporary materials, integrated coffee preparation equipment, and a central degustation area to create a refined setting for product presentation, interaction, and hospitality."}],"photos":5},"bd-promotors-offices-barcelona":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The corporate offices of BD Promotors in Barcelona reflect a sophisticated and timeless approach to workplace design. The project combines elegant materials, metallic finishes, wood panelling and contemporary furniture to create a prestigious corporate environment."},{"type":"p","text":"The layout integrates an impressive reception area, executive offices, meeting rooms and comfortable lounge spaces. Architectural lighting, customized decorative features and corporate branding reinforce the company’s identity."},{"type":"p","text":"The result is a refined and functional workplace designed to convey professionalism, exclusivity and corporate excellence."}],"photos":6},"carl-zeiss-academy-africa-johannesburg-south-africa":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"ZEISS Academy Africa – Training &amp; Experience Centre"},{"type":"p","text":"Design &amp; Build | Learning, Innovation &amp; Technology"},{"type":"p","text":"ZEISS Academy Africa is a modern training and experience centre designed to support professional development, knowledge sharing and hands-on learning for ZEISS customers and partners."},{"type":"p","text":"The project combines specialized technical training laboratories, interactive demonstration areas and collaborative learning spaces, creating an environment where advanced optical technology meets contemporary interior design."},{"type":"p","text":"The interior features dedicated workstations equipped with ZEISS optical and ophthalmic instruments, flexible training areas, integrated audiovisual systems and carefully designed lighting solutions. The distinctive ZEISS blue accents reinforce the corporate identity, while glass partitions, natural materials, comfortable breakout areas and greenery create a welcoming and inspiring atmosphere."},{"type":"p","text":"Designed to accommodate a wide range of educational activities, from practical equipment training and workshops to digital learning and professional presentations, the Academy offers a flexible environment that encourages interaction, innovation and knowledge exchange."}],"photos":6},"glovo-headquarters-warsaw":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"GLOVO – Warsaw Headquarters"},{"type":"p","text":"Design &amp; Build | 1,400 m² | Warsaw, Poland"},{"type":"p","text":"BEPLAN delivered a modern, dynamic workplace for Glovo in Warsaw, designed to encourage collaboration, flexibility and employee wellbeing."},{"type":"p","text":"The 1,400 m² project combines open-plan workstations, meeting rooms, focus areas, collaborative spaces and a spacious auditorium for company presentations and events. Social zones, comfortable lounges and a contemporary kitchen create an inviting environment for informal meetings and everyday interaction."},{"type":"p","text":"The interior features natural wood finishes, exposed installations, acoustic solutions, extensive greenery and carefully selected furniture, complemented by Glovo’s distinctive corporate identity."},{"type":"p","text":"The result is a vibrant, functional and inspiring workplace that reflects Glovo’s innovative culture while balancing productivity, comfort and collaboration."}],"photos":6},"carl-zeiss-offices-dubai-uae":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"CARL ZEISS – DUBAI, UAE"},{"type":"p","text":"Corporate Headquarters &amp; Vision Showroom | 1,500 m²"},{"type":"p","text":"Located in Dubai’s Medical District, the Carl Zeiss project involved the integration and refurbishment of two existing offices into a unified, modern workplace covering approximately 1,500 m²."},{"type":"p","text":"The objective was to create a cohesive and functional environment that reflects Carl Zeiss’s corporate identity, commitment to innovation, and leadership in optical technology, while providing flexible and comfortable spaces for employees, clients, and visitors."},{"type":"p","text":"The project combines open-plan workspaces, private offices, meeting rooms, phone booths, collaborative areas, and social spaces, supporting different working styles and encouraging communication, productivity, and employee well-being."},{"type":"p","text":"A key feature of the project is the Vision Showroom, a dedicated space designed to showcase Carl Zeiss’s advanced optical technologies and vision-care solutions. The showroom integrates specialized equipment, interactive displays, and distinctive architectural elements to create an engaging experience for visitors and clients."},{"type":"p","text":"The interior design follows a contemporary architectural language, combining clean lines, glass partitions, customized joinery, acoustic solutions, integrated lighting, and carefully selected materials. Corporate branding and optical-inspired visual elements reinforce the company’s identity throughout the space."},{"type":"p","text":"Particular attention was given to the integration of the two previously independent offices, ensuring visual continuity, efficient circulation, and coordinated technical infrastructure."},{"type":"p","text":"The result is a modern, multifunctional corporate environment that brings together technology, workplace efficiency, and architectural design, reflecting Carl Zeiss’s global standards and innovative spirit."},{"type":"p","text":"Project Details"},{"type":"p","text":"Client: Carl Zeiss"},{"type":"p","text":"Location: Dubai Medical District, UAE"},{"type":"p","text":"Area: Approximately 1,500 m²"},{"type":"p","text":"Project Type: Corporate Office Integration &amp; Vision Showroom"},{"type":"p","text":"Scope: Integration of two existing offices, office refurbishment, workplace design, open-plan workstations, meeting rooms, phone booths, collaborative spaces, social areas, and specialized Vision Showroom."}],"photos":6},"galeria-gastronomica-barcelona":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Galería Gastronómica – Barcelona"},{"type":"p","text":"Interior Design &amp; Art Collaboration | Estrella Salietti &amp; Lorenzo Quinn"},{"type":"p","text":"Galería Gastronómica was a distinctive restaurant and art gallery inaugurated in Barcelona, combining fine dining, contemporary art and sophisticated interior design."},{"type":"p","text":"The project was developed in collaboration with renowned interior designer Estrella Salietti and featured sculptural works by internationally acclaimed artist Lorenzo Quinn."},{"type":"p","text":"The interior combined natural stone, exposed concrete columns, warm ambient lighting, glass elements and carefully integrated artworks to create an elegant, intimate atmosphere. The restaurant was conceived as a meeting point between gastronomy and artistic expression, with exhibition spaces integrated into the dining experience."}],"photos":6},"transporeon-poland":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Interior Design and Functionality Transporeon’s offices combine a modern and functional design with an environment that promotes well-being and sustainability. The furniture was supplied by Alea, including Blade meeting tables, Atreo workstations with acoustic panels, and Atreo Wood high tables for the break areas. During the construction phase, solutions such as glass and plasterboard partitions, wood, ceramic, moss, and wallpaper cladding, raised floors, and suspended acoustic ceilings were implemented."},{"type":"p","text":"Adaptation to Collaborative Work During the renovation, Transporeon adapted its offices to encourage teamwork and collaboration between departments. Functional meeting areas, coworking spaces, and private offices were created, addressing the diverse needs of employees."},{"type":"p","text":"Sustainable Environment The Porto Office complex was built following sustainability principles and is LEED certified."}],"photos":6},"tik-tok-bytedance-offices":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Project: ByteDance – 11th Floor Fit-Out Location: Grzybowska 60, Warsaw"},{"type":"p","text":"The works comprise the partial refurbishment and reconfiguration of the existing 11th floor office space within the area indicated by the blue dotted line (scope boundary) on the drawings."},{"type":"p","text":"The project includes demolition, construction of new partitioned areas, modifications to MEP services, lighting adjustments, AV relocations, flooring works, and installation of new furniture to accommodate the proposed layouts (Option 1 / Option 2)."},{"type":"p","text":"All dimensions, power provisions, and compliance requirements are to be verified on site prior to execution. Works must comply with local codes, fire strategy, and building regulations."}],"photos":5},"olly-offices":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Office design proposal for Olly: an inspiring environment with a biophilic approach, open-plan layout, and strategic areas to enhance interaction and creativity."}],"photos":6},"bloober-offices":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The office design is dynamic, modern, and conducive to creativity, making it ideal for a software company. The combination of collaborative spaces, functional workstations, and a well-crafted aesthetic creates an environment that fosters both productivity and innovation."}],"photos":6},"embassy-coffee":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Thoughtfully Designed for Comfort and StyleThis coffee shop is a seamless blend of modern aesthetics and inviting comfort. Every element has been carefully considered—from the clean, minimalist lines of the furniture to the abundance of natural light that floods the space through large windows. Warm wood finishes and soft, earthy tones create a welcoming atmosphere that feels both contemporary and cozy. The layout is intentionally balanced to support a variety of experiences: communal tables encourage social connection and collaboration, while quiet corners and plush seating provide a peaceful retreat for reading, working, or relaxing. Whether you’re meeting a friend, catching up on emails, or simply enjoying a cup of coffee, the space is designed to enhance your experience through thoughtful details and timeless style."}],"photos":6},"carl-zeiss-headquarters":{"blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"ZEISS Meditec S.A.S. | Paris, France"},{"type":"p","text":"The ZEISS Meditec office project in Marly combines contemporary workplace design with functionality, comfort and a strong corporate identity."},{"type":"p","text":"The space features bright open-plan workstations, meeting rooms, collaborative areas and informal breakout spaces. Clean architectural lines, glazed partitions and integrated lighting create a professional and welcoming environment, while carefully selected materials, acoustic solutions and ZEISS-branded graphics reinforce the company’s identity."},{"type":"p","text":"A balance of technical precision, flexibility and employee well-being defines a workplace designed to support collaboration, productivity and everyday operations."}],"photos":6},"lawyers-office":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Lawyer’s Office Design – Elegant, Wooden Luxury with Marble Accents"},{"type":"p","text":"The office exudes a timeless, professional atmosphere with a foundation rooted in natural materials and high-end finishes. The space is primarily crafted from rich, dark-toned wood — think walnut or mahogany — which frames the entire setting in warmth and refinement."},{"type":"h","text":"Reception Area"},{"type":"p","text":"Upon entering, visitors are greeted by a custom-built wood-paneled reception desk with a smooth marble countertop — white with subtle grey veining. Behind the desk, a full-height bookshelf wall with integrated lighting showcases leather-bound law books and curated decorative objects. The walls are clad in wooden panels with inlaid brass trim, adding a touch of classic luxury."},{"type":"h","text":"Flooring"},{"type":"p","text":"Throughout the office, a finely crafted wooden parquet floor adds texture and elegance — arranged in herringbone or chevron patterns for visual interest. The wood has a satin finish, emphasizing the grain without overpowering the space. Area rugs in muted tones define seating areas and dampen acoustics, enhancing comfort."},{"type":"h","text":"Main Office / Partner’s Room"},{"type":"p","text":"The main office is a statement of prestige:"},{"type":"li","text":"A massive wooden desk with carved detailing and a marble inset surface commands attention."},{"type":"li","text":"Floor-to-ceiling bookshelves line one wall, while another features wood-framed glass cabinetry to display accolades, legal awards, or curated artifacts."},{"type":"li","text":"A fireplace with a marble mantle provides a classic focal point (even if purely decorative)."},{"type":"li","text":"Leather armchairs and a low marble coffee table create a client seating area, bathed in warm, natural light from tall windows framed with linen drapes and wood valances."},{"type":"h","text":"Conference Room"},{"type":"p","text":"This space combines power and polish:"},{"type":"li","text":"A long wooden table, custom-made with marble inlays and leather blotters, seats up to 10."},{"type":"li","text":"High-backed chairs in dark leather complement the table."},{"type":"li","text":"A marble feature wall, possibly used as a backdrop for the firm’s name or logo, adds visual weight."},{"type":"li","text":"Subtle recessed lighting and a custom chandelier with brass and glass elements provide soft but sophisticated illumination."},{"type":"h","text":"Details &amp; Atmosphere"},{"type":"li","text":"Brass hardware, handcrafted moldings, and leather wall insets reinforce the luxurious theme."},{"type":"li","text":"Lighting includes warm LED sconces, desk lamps with marble bases, and ambient indirect lights tucked into wooden ceiling coffers."},{"type":"li","text":"Carefully chosen art pieces — legal-themed or abstract works — add personality without distraction."}],"photos":6},"club-uno-barcelona":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Club Uno, Barcelona is a design &amp; build project conceived as a bold, immersive nightlife venue with a strong contemporary identity. The space combines dramatic red and black tones, atmospheric lighting, intimate lounge seating, and a stylish bar area to create a sophisticated yet energetic club experience. Carefully designed to enhance mood, movement, and social interaction, Club Uno offers a distinctive environment that blends comfort, visual impact, and a vibrant urban character."}],"photos":6},"carl-zeiss-headquarters-lisbon":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Design and Construction of Corporate Offices for Carl Zeiss AG, Lisbon"},{"type":"p","text":"Working closely with the Global Real Estate Manager of Carl Zeiss AG, we led the design and construction of their new corporate offices in Lisbon. The project was executed in full accordance with Zeiss’s global design and operational standards, ensuring the new workspace reflects the company’s international brand identity while addressing local functional needs and cultural context."}],"photos":6},"groupon-headquarters-6th-floor":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Project: Groupon – Atlas Tower, WarsawScope: Comprehensive Interior Renovation"},{"type":"p","text":"We executed a full-scale interior renovation for Groupon’s offices located in the Atlas Tower in Warsaw. The primary objective was to transform the existing workspace into a modern, functional environment that fosters employee well-being, productivity, and collaboration."},{"type":"p","text":"Our design and execution focused on several key elements:"},{"type":"li","text":"Workspace Optimization: We reconfigured the office layout to support various work styles, introducing flexible open-plan areas, quiet zones, and collaborative spaces tailored to team dynamics."},{"type":"li","text":"Employee Comfort: Special attention was given to ergonomics, acoustics, lighting, and indoor climate, ensuring that all elements contributed to a healthier and more pleasant work atmosphere."},{"type":"li","text":"Aesthetic Refresh: A contemporary design palette was applied, blending Groupon’s brand identity with clean lines, natural materials, and vibrant accents to create an inspiring and cohesive interior."},{"type":"li","text":"Functional Upgrades: We modernized meeting rooms, social areas, and amenities, incorporating the latest AV and IT infrastructure to support seamless communication and efficient workflows."},{"type":"li","text":"Sustainability: Environmentally friendly materials and energy-efficient solutions were prioritized to align with Groupon’s corporate sustainability values."},{"type":"p","text":"The result is a revitalized office environment that not only reflects Groupon’s dynamic corporate culture but also enhances the overall workplace experience for its employees."}],"photos":6},"pzu":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Beplan has recently finished an office fit out for PZU in Wroclaw. The project is located in Quattro Forum building. To meet the standards of the client, new walls, suspended ceilings, lightning fixtures and IT installation were done completely new. Vibrant workspaces promote positive culture, strengthen core values and shape future direction. An attractively designed kitchen with resting areas put an accent in cooperation and communication between employees."}],"photos":6},"iwg-coworking":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"This space was born as a collaborative space designed to inspire productivity, creativity, and a strong sense of community. More than just a physical location, it embodies a philosophy of openness, innovation, and human connection. The environment is thoughtfully curated to encourage interaction and idea exchange, while also offering quiet corners for focused work and reflection."},{"type":"p","text":"The interior design draws from a warm industrial aesthetic, merging the raw, honest character of materials like smoothed concrete, exposed steel beams, and industrial lighting with the natural comfort of wood accents and textured finishes. This balance creates a visually striking yet welcoming atmosphere. The furniture features clean lines and ergonomic design, crafted from natural wood to bring warmth and organic texture to the space. Wall coverings, shelving, and communal tables are also made with wood finishes, enhancing the tactile and visual richness of the environment."},{"type":"p","text":"Natural light is a key feature, flooding the open-plan layout through large windows and skylights, reinforcing a connection to the outdoors and boosting well-being. Greenery is thoughtfully integrated, softening the industrial elements and adding life to the space."},{"type":"p","text":"Not just a workplace—it’s a dynamic ecosystem where freelancers, startups, and established professionals come together, driven by the shared goal of building meaningful work in a space that feels alive, authentic, and collaborative."}],"photos":6},"wework-bacardi":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Our team was entrusted with the complete design and fit-out of a new WeWork office location in the heart of Warsaw, Poland. This project involved transforming a raw commercial space into a vibrant, fully operational coworking environment that reflects the WeWork brand’s global standards while integrating local flair."},{"type":"p","text":"From the initial concept development and space planning to the final interior finishes and furniture installation, we delivered a turnkey solution that emphasizes flexibility, comfort, and style. The fit-out included private offices, shared desks, meeting rooms, breakout areas, kitchens, and phone booths — all designed to encourage collaboration and creativity."}],"photos":6},"groupon-headquarters-8th-floor":{"blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"Groupon’s Warsaw headquarters, located in the iconic Atlas Tower, is a dynamic and forward-thinking workspace that reflects the company’s innovative spirit and global identity. The design blends functionality with a playful aesthetic, offering a collaborative and energizing environment for over [insert number] employees."},{"type":"h","text":"Design Concept"},{"type":"p","text":"The interior design emphasizes openness, connectivity, and comfort, aligning with Groupon’s tech-driven, people-first culture. The layout integrates open-plan work areas, versatile meeting spaces, quiet zones, and social hubs to support diverse working styles."},{"type":"p","text":"Key features include:"},{"type":"li","text":"Branded Visual Identity: Bold colors, custom graphics, and environmental branding elements reinforce the Groupon ethos."},{"type":"li","text":"Flexible Workspaces: Adjustable desks, breakout zones, and collaborative areas enhance agility and productivity."},{"type":"li","text":"Biophilic Elements: Natural materials and abundant greenery contribute to employee well-being and environmental quality."},{"type":"li","text":"Acoustic Solutions: Sound-absorbing panels and enclosed phone booths provide acoustic comfort in a bustling workspace."},{"type":"h","text":"Materials &amp; Lighting"},{"type":"p","text":"A combination of industrial textures—exposed ceilings, polished concrete, and metal details—are softened by wood finishes and textile accents. Strategic lighting design creates a balanced atmosphere between task illumination and ambient mood."},{"type":"h","text":"Sustainability"},{"type":"p","text":"The project incorporates eco-conscious materials and energy-efficient lighting, aligning with Groupon’s commitment to sustainability and corporate responsibility."}],"photos":6},"chep-polska-main-headquarters":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"1.400 sqm office design and fit out in Mokotow Business Center."},{"type":"p","text":"Chep is a logistics pooling company that needed to change its way of working into an open space to operate more efficiently. We designed a office, where people can interact and communicate seamlessly, and meeting spaces for presentations and board meetings."},{"type":"p","text":"Collaboration shouldn’t just happen in meetings, It should happen effortlessly in informal interactions in lounge areas, team spaces, project rooms, and throughout the day as people communicate easily in this open office. Private spaces for focus or private conversations are equally important, of course, and it’s important to provide space where small collaborations can break off from larger groups."},{"type":"p","text":"The flooring is predominantly made up of light blue &amp; deep blue coloured carpet through the main office floors varying in different areas. Some accent in colour had been added in the meeting rooms. To the far end of the layout there is a staff break-out zone, with comfortable seating &amp; fixed booth seating."}],"photos":6},"carl-zeiss-offices":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"We delivered a comprehensive office design and fit-out for ZEISS in Paris, creating a modern workspace that reflects the company’s commitment to innovation, precision, and technological excellence. The goal was to design an environment that supports both focused individual work and seamless collaboration, while staying true to ZEISS’s global brand identity."},{"type":"p","text":"The layout includes open-plan workstations, quiet zones, meeting rooms equipped with state-of-the-art AV systems, and a welcoming reception area that communicates professionalism and clarity from the moment you enter. Carefully selected materials, lighting, and finishes highlight the brand’s clean, high-tech aesthetic while enhancing acoustic comfort and user experience."},{"type":"p","text":"Sustainability and ergonomics were core principles throughout the project. From energy-efficient lighting to height-adjustable desks and breathable materials, every detail was chosen with employee well-being and long-term performance in mind."},{"type":"p","text":"Working closely with ZEISS’s local and international teams, we ensured the final result met strict corporate standards, as well as local building regulations and cultural nuances. The new Paris office is a future-ready workspace tailored to the needs of a global technology leader."}],"photos":6},"nespresso-main-offices":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Worldwide espresso company Nespresso added an office in Warsaw with the help of our design firm."},{"type":"p","text":"A colourful palette of painting defines the complete scheme: all warm and clear, allowing the light to refract: wood, glass, white melamine and MDF. Each company department is distinguished by its own colour. These colours are inspired in the all famous capsule coffee manufactured by Nespresso. All partitions are made in glass with grey vinyl contouring the company logo so the natural light fills all the spaces."}],"photos":6},"eiffage-polska-main-headquarters":{"blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Design Concept for Eiffage Poland Headquarters:"},{"type":"p","text":"The design for the Eiffage Poland Headquarters combines a modern industrial aesthetic with warm touches of natural wood to create an inviting yet professional environment. The space is crafted to inspire collaboration, innovation, and productivity while offering a dynamic and flexible workplace for employees. The open-plan office layout encourages interaction, while private and semi-private spaces provide flexibility for various work styles."},{"type":"h","text":"Key Features:"},{"type":"h","text":"1. Open Space Layout:"},{"type":"p","text":"The heart of the headquarters is an expansive open-plan office. The layout fosters collaboration and communication between teams, with carefully placed workstations to maintain a sense of openness. The design is fluid and adaptable, ensuring employees can move freely and interact with colleagues. Work areas are thoughtfully arranged to maximize light and provide a comfortable, ergonomic workspace for all employees."},{"type":"h","text":"2. Glassed Meeting Rooms:"},{"type":"p","text":"Strategically placed throughout the space, glazed meeting rooms offer privacy without compromising the open feel. The transparent glass walls allow for natural light to flow freely across the office, promoting a bright, airy atmosphere. These rooms are equipped with state-of-the-art audiovisual technology to facilitate both formal and informal meetings, and they are designed to be easily reconfigured to suit different needs."},{"type":"h","text":"3. Wooden Elements for Warmth:"},{"type":"p","text":"Wooden elements are subtly integrated throughout the design to balance the industrial, modern aesthetics. Wooden panels, flooring accents, and furniture bring a natural warmth to the space, creating a welcoming and comfortable environment for employees. The rich textures of the wood soften the otherwise minimalist, industrial design and add an organic touch to the office."},{"type":"h","text":"4. Industrial Modern Look:"},{"type":"p","text":"The industrial style is reflected in the exposed concrete ceilings, steel fixtures, and raw materials such as metal and glass. The use of industrial lighting fixtures, like exposed bulbs and metal pendant lights, adds to the urban feel of the space. Large windows provide abundant natural light and emphasize the spaciousness of the open plan, while enhancing the connection to the surrounding environment."},{"type":"h","text":"5. Social Areas:"},{"type":"p","text":"Designed for relaxation and socialization, the social areas include comfortable lounges, kitchenettes, and casual seating arrangements. These spaces are strategically placed to encourage spontaneous interactions, networking, and downtime. Soft furnishings, such as plush couches and seating clusters, are paired with vibrant, informal decor to create a relaxed atmosphere where employees can unwind or connect in an informal setting."},{"type":"h","text":"6. Informal Meeting Spaces:"},{"type":"p","text":"In addition to formal meeting rooms, there are several informal meeting spaces scattered throughout the headquarters. These areas are equipped with comfortable seating, writable walls, and flexible layouts, making them perfect for brainstorming sessions, quick catch-ups, or collaborative work. The informal meeting spaces are designed to be cozy and inspiring, fostering creativity and teamwork in a less structured environment."},{"type":"h","text":"7. Biophilic Design:"},{"type":"p","text":"To further enhance the work environment, biophilic design principles are incorporated, such as the inclusion of indoor plants and natural materials. These elements help reduce stress, improve air quality, and connect the space to nature, which is vital for employee well-being and productivity."},{"type":"h","text":"Overall Aesthetic:"},{"type":"p","text":"The headquarters seamlessly integrates modern industrial elements with warmth and comfort. The design fosters a collaborative and flexible atmosphere, where employees feel empowered and inspired. The careful balance of open spaces, private meeting rooms, and social areas ensures that every type of work can be performed efficiently, from focused tasks to team collaboration. The modern industrial style, combined with the natural beauty of wood and biophilic touches, creates a space that feels both dynamic and grounded."},{"type":"p","text":"This design concept provides an inspiring and functional environment for Eiffage Poland, blending contemporary industrial design with thoughtful, human-centered elements. Let me know if you’d like to expand on any specific details or make changes!"}],"photos":6},"hoegl-shoe-fashion":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Project Overview: The design project for Högl Shoe Fashion in the Designer Outlet, Piaseczno, focuses on creating a sophisticated and modern retail space that reflects the brand’s Austrian heritage and dedication to craftsmanship, comfort, and contemporary elegance. The goal was to offer a welcoming and luxurious environment that enhances the customer experience and highlights the premium quality of Högl’s footwear collections."},{"type":"p","text":"Design Concept: The concept draws inspiration from the brand’s core values—elegance, femininity, and simplicity. The design emphasizes clean lines, a neutral color palette with soft accents, and high-quality materials such as brushed metals, oak wood finishes, and velvet textiles to create a refined, tactile experience. Custom shelving and display units were designed to showcase products with elegance while maintaining optimal accessibility and flow."},{"type":"p","text":"Outcome: The final design offers a seamless blend of style and function, reinforcing Högl’s position as a premium footwear brand. It stands out within the outlet setting, drawing attention through understated elegance and thoughtful spatial planning."}],"photos":6},"restaurant-in-madrid":{"blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"TELIRIUM RESTAURANT | BARCELONA"},{"type":"p","text":"Located in Barcelona’s Les Corts district, Telirium was a contemporary restaurant combining Mediterranean cuisine with a refined and welcoming atmosphere. The interior design featured elegant materials, modern furnishings, and versatile dining areas, including private spaces and an outdoor terrace."},{"type":"p","text":"I participated in the interior design in collaboration with renowned Barcelona-based designer Estrella Salietti, contributing to the creation of a sophisticated and functional hospitality environment."}],"photos":6},"groupon-headquarters-7th-floor":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Project for Groupon – Atlas Tower, WarsawWe executed a comprehensive interior renovation for Groupon’s offices located in Atlas Tower, focusing on enhancing employee comfort, collaboration, and overall workplace experience."},{"type":"p","text":"Scope of Work:"},{"type":"li","text":"New Resting and Social Areas:We designed and built modern, comfortable spaces for relaxation and informal interaction. These areas include lounge seating, soft lighting, and biophilic elements to promote well-being and foster spontaneous collaboration among teams."},{"type":"li","text":"New Kitchens and Dining Spaces:Fully equipped kitchenettes and dining zones were installed on multiple floors to provide convenient, welcoming areas for employees to gather during breaks or lunch hours. Finishes included high-end cabinetry, quartz countertops, and contemporary lighting fixtures to match the office’s aesthetic."},{"type":"li","text":"Suspended Acoustic Panels:To address noise control and improve acoustic comfort, we installed a system of suspended acoustic panels in key open-plan areas. These not only enhance sound quality but also contribute a modern design element to the ceiling space."},{"type":"p","text":"Objective:The project aimed to upgrade shared spaces, encouraging a more collaborative and engaging work environment aligned with Groupon’s dynamic company culture."}],"photos":6},"residence-of-the-ambassador-of-the-republic-of-indonesia":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The design and construction of the Indonesian Ambassador’s Residence in Warsaw is an extraordinary project, a four-story single-family home that harmoniously blends traditional Indonesian architectural elements with modern design. This residence reflects the rich cultural heritage of Indonesia while embracing contemporary comforts and functionality."},{"type":"p","text":"The floors are elegantly finished with marble, adding a sense of luxury and sophistication to the entire residence. The walls are adorned with high-quality, upholstered fabric, creating a soft, refined atmosphere throughout the space."},{"type":"p","text":"The residence includes six bathrooms, each designed with exquisite attention to detail, incorporating high-end fixtures and finishes to ensure both style and comfort. The spacious living room is an open and airy area, ideal for both relaxation and entertaining, with large windows offering ample natural light."},{"type":"p","text":"In total, the residence features seven bedrooms, two of which are specifically designed as guest rooms, offering privacy and comfort for visitors. Each room is carefully designed with unique touches that reflect the traditional Indonesian aesthetic, such as intricate woodwork and artisanal craftsmanship, while still maintaining a modern flair."},{"type":"p","text":"The overall architectural design and interior layout of the residence represent a seamless fusion of cultural heritage and modern luxury, making it a truly unique and exceptional home for the Ambassador."}],"photos":6},"carl-zeiss-warsaw":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Design, Management, and Construction of Carl Zeiss Corporate Project"},{"type":"p","text":"The project encompassed the comprehensive design, technical supervision, and full execution of works for the new corporate facilities of Carl Zeiss, a global leader in optical and precision technology. The space was conceived as a multifunctional hub that addresses both operational needs and the company’s high standards for technology and aesthetics."},{"type":"p","text":"Program and Space Distribution"},{"type":"p","text":"The new facility includes:"},{"type":"li","text":"A fully equipped training center for technical instruction and specialized workshops."},{"type":"li","text":"Multiple meeting rooms of various sizes, fitted with state-of-the-art audiovisual systems."},{"type":"li","text":"Open-space work areas designed to encourage collaboration and team interaction."},{"type":"li","text":"Private offices for executive functions and focused work."},{"type":"li","text":"A dedicated technical laboratory tailored for Zeiss precision machinery, featuring structural stability, environmental control, and sound insulation."},{"type":"p","text":"Interior Design and Finishes"},{"type":"li","text":"The design uses a neutral and elegant color palette, dominated by graphite gray and white, accented with the iconic Zeiss blue to reflect the company’s visual identity."},{"type":"li","text":"Floors are covered with modular gray carpet tiles, offering both acoustic comfort and a professional, contemporary look."},{"type":"li","text":"Suspended acoustic ceiling panels were integrated to enhance sound performance while adding a refined architectural language."},{"type":"li","text":"Full-height glass partitions were used to bring in natural light and visual transparency, while preserving spatial separation and privacy."},{"type":"li","text":"White lacquered doors with brushed steel hardware complement the sleek and functional design."},{"type":"li","text":"The laboratory is equipped with technical flooring and specialized furniture, adapted for precision equipment and outfitted with concealed electrical and data infrastructure for a clean and safe workspace."},{"type":"p","text":"Overall Concept"},{"type":"p","text":"The design was guided by principles of efficiency, innovation, and brand representation. Special attention was paid to the integration of technology, ergonomics, and aesthetics, with a sustainable approach to both material selection and construction solutions."}],"photos":6},"carl-zeiss":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Design and office fit out for Carl Zeiss AG. Working with its Global Real Estate Manager, we designed its offices in Poznań, Poland."}],"photos":6},"elli-lilly-main-offices":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"In cooperation with HOK London, we produced the execution design and fit out of Elli Lilly’s headquarters in Warsaw."},{"type":"p","text":"The space needed to reflect the company brand values of innovation and passion. The new office creates an engaging and dynamic environment for the Elli Lilly team, potential employees, and visitors."},{"type":"p","text":"The textured carpet, wall acoustic coverings, and custom colored light fixtures create a layered sophistication with every surface thoughtfully considered."},{"type":"p","text":"We’ve created a palette of place: a range of owned and shared spaces designed for both individual work and team work. This concept leads to workplaces that allow people to choose where and how they want to work, or as we call it, “best place”."}],"photos":6},"trinity-park-main-reception-area":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"TRINITY PARK | Reception Area | Warsaw"},{"type":"p","text":"BEPLAN Design + Build developed a comprehensive architectural and interior design concept for the main reception area of Trinity Park, a modern office complex in Warsaw."},{"type":"p","text":"The project focuses on transforming the entrance lobby into a sophisticated, welcoming, and representative space that enhances the building’s identity and overall visitor experience."},{"type":"p","text":"The design combines contemporary architectural elements, elegant finishes, bespoke reception furniture, integrated greenery, and carefully planned lighting to create a refined and harmonious environment."},{"type":"p","text":"Special attention was given to spatial organization, circulation, material selection, and architectural detailing, ensuring a seamless balance between aesthetics, functionality, and comfort."},{"type":"p","text":"The result is a distinctive, timeless reception area that reinforces the building’s corporate character while creating a strong first impression for tenants and visitors."}],"photos":6},"zlota-44-level-46":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"This exceptional 220 square meter apartment, located on the 46th floor of the iconic Złota 44 building, offers a rare combination of luxury, elegance, and panoramic views of Warsaw’s skyline"},{"type":"p","text":"The expansive living areas are laid with rich American walnut wood flooring, offering a warm and inviting contrast to the contemporary interior. Each board is carefully selected and arranged to highlight the natural grain and texture of the wood, creating a seamless and elegant foundation for the home."},{"type":"p","text":"The bathrooms are finished in exquisite white Carrara marble, a classic Italian stone renowned for its clean lines and subtle veining. The marble surfaces — including floors, walls, and countertops — reflect a refined sense of luxury and purity, turning everyday routines into spa-like experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"All fittings are by Dornbracht, a German manufacturer celebrated for its precision engineering and cutting-edge design. These high-end fixtures not only ensure durability and performance but also add a sculptural quality to the bathrooms and kitchen."},{"type":"p","text":"Every piece of furniture in the apartment is custom-made, tailored to fit the space and crafted with premium materials. From built-in cabinetry to statement furnishings, each item reflects a commitment to quality, function, and design harmony. The overall aesthetic is one of understated elegance, where comfort meets contemporary style."},{"type":"p","text":"This apartment is a rare opportunity to experience luxury living at its finest in one of Warsaw’s most prestigious residential addresses."}],"photos":6},"mbank-senatorska":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"mBank – Senatorska, Warsaw"},{"type":"p","text":"Office Interior Design &amp; Build | BEPLAN Design + Build"},{"type":"p","text":"The mBank office project on Senatorska Street in Warsaw represents a modern workplace environment that combines functionality, employee comfort, and a distinctive corporate identity."},{"type":"p","text":"The interior design integrates open-plan workspaces, meeting rooms, and collaborative areas, creating a flexible and efficient working environment. Glass partitions maximize natural light and visual transparency, while acoustic solutions enhance privacy and everyday working comfort."},{"type":"p","text":"The interior is characterized by contemporary furniture, geometric carpet patterns, carefully selected lighting, and vibrant color accents inspired by mBank’s corporate identity. Greenery and thoughtfully integrated architectural details contribute to a welcoming, dynamic, and professional atmosphere."},{"type":"p","text":"The result is a functional and contemporary workplace designed to encourage collaboration, productivity, and employee well-being."}],"photos":6},"sttas-europe-main-offices":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"STTAS – 1,600 m² Office Design | Business Garden"},{"type":"p","text":"Client: Vastint | Location: Business Garden, Poland"},{"type":"p","text":"Commissioned by Vastint, we designed STTAS’s 1,600 m² office in the Business Garden complex, developing a modern and flexible workplace based on the concept of the “Interconnected Workplace.”"},{"type":"p","text":"The design balances privacy, productivity, and collaboration through a combination of open workspaces, private offices, and glass partitions that maximize natural light."},{"type":"p","text":"Vibrant breakout areas, kitchens, and informal meeting spaces encourage interaction and creativity, while carefully selected materials, colors, and furnishings create a welcoming and inspiring working environment."},{"type":"p","text":"The result is a functional, contemporary office that reflects STTAS’s corporate identity while promoting employee well-being, flexibility, and collaboration."}],"photos":6},"t-mobile":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Following Deutsche Telekom’s acquisition of Era, the office was reimagined under the T-Mobile brand, with the goal of creating a fresh, modern and inspiring workplace fully aligned with the company’s brand standards and identity."},{"type":"p","text":"The concept was developed not only to reflect the new visual language of T-Mobile, but also to create an environment that would motivate employees, support collaboration and express the values of the business. The design combines strong branding, functional planning and a lively atmosphere, resulting in a workspace that feels both professional and energizing."},{"type":"p","text":"To give the office a clear identity and create a more dynamic experience throughout the building, each floor was assigned its own distinct color theme. Starting with the iconic corporate magenta on the ground floor, the upper levels were differentiated through a palette of greens, blues, yellows and oranges. This approach helped create a strong visual character for every level while also improving wayfinding and giving each area its own personality."},{"type":"p","text":"The use of color was carefully considered from both a branding and psychological perspective. We know that different colors can influence mood, energy and behavior, so brighter and more vivid tones were introduced in breakout areas, informal meeting spaces and social zones, encouraging creativity, interaction and a more relaxed atmosphere. In contrast, corridors, focused workspaces and management areas were designed with calmer greys, whites and neutral tones, creating a more balanced and professional environment suitable for concentration and day-to-day work."},{"type":"p","text":"Large-format graphics, feature walls and branded visual elements were integrated throughout the office to strengthen the identity of the space and make it more engaging. Informal lounges, meeting points and breakout areas were designed as places where employees could step away from their desks, recharge, meet colleagues or have casual discussions in a more relaxed setting."}],"photos":6},"idg-poland-sa-main-offices":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The main activity of the company focuses, among others, on the organization of technology conferences, recruitment of participants for events, organization, e-seminars and e-debates, research expertise, content and email marketing."},{"type":"p","text":"The simple color palette, red black and grey, accentuates the space’s clean lines and sleek finishes. From the lighting approach to the wall covering with graphics, we created a space for cooperation and openness."},{"type":"p","text":"In addition to the architectural work, there was also graphic work done which is expressed on the office walls, and which was inspired by the world of technology."},{"type":"p","text":"The overall look and feel of the space is reflective of IDG’s culture: modern, forward-thinking and innovative."}],"photos":6},"bouygues-immobilier-main-offices":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The design of Bouygues Immobilier headquearters was done in two stages. Firstly, the ground floor, was transformed into the main reception area for meetings and customers. We re-designed in a way to accommodate four new meeting rooms and an area for clients to view samples of materials used on their apartments."},{"type":"p","text":"The first floor hosts the main office area, with an open space layout, and workstations placed in groups of 6 people. The open environment provides employees with choice and flexibility between a variety of work spaces — from individual workstations to open and enclosed meeting areas and “quiet rooms” for individual work or small group meetings. This flexibility and the inspiring design of the space has created a new sense of energy and collaboration reflecting Bouygues Immobilier continued growth and evolution as a firm."}],"photos":6},"house-c":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A stunning, modern two-story house with a minimalist yet warm architectural design. The structure combines exposed concrete with wood accents, giving it a sophisticated, earthy appeal. Large floor-to-ceiling windows dominate both floors, allowing abundant natural light to flood the interior and enhancing the connection between the indoor and outdoor spaces."}],"photos":6},"residential-apartments":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Modern residential apartment building with a sleek, contemporary design. It is a five-story structure characterized by a white facade accented with vertical wooden panels and large glass windows. Each apartment features spacious balconies with transparent glass railings, adding to the building’s open and airy aesthetic."}],"photos":6},"nestle-retail-learning-center":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Combining leading consumer and shopper research with cutting edge digital technology, the centres are used to demonstrate how people behave when shopping and when using Nestlé products at home."},{"type":"p","text":"This followed a series of brainstorming meetings with key members of the company who told us they wanted a place that was inspiring, visually exciting and a where people would like to meet. We designed a 950 sqm. Retail learning center to promote the company´s products among their wholesalers with a space divided in technological rooms, presentation and meeting areas."}],"photos":6},"unicredit-main-headquarters":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Unicredit, one of Poland’s leading banks, entrusted us with the design and fit-out of their new office space located in the Mokotów Business Center, within the prestigious Business Garden complex in Warsaw."},{"type":"p","text":"The design concept reflects Unicredit’s corporate identity through the strategic use of their bold color palette in graphics, signage, and wayfinding elements. These visual cues not only enhance brand presence but also serve as navigational aids throughout the office."},{"type":"p","text":"To foster a more collaborative and employee-friendly environment, the project included the creation of modern meeting rooms, as well as dedicated resting and relaxation areas. Vibrant wall graphics and custom wallpapers were installed to bring energy and character to the workspace, making it more dynamic and engaging."}],"photos":6},"pbt":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"mBank MCO | Park Business Teofilów | Łódź, Poland"},{"type":"p","text":"4,000 m² | 5 Floors | Design &amp; Build / General Contracting"},{"type":"p","text":"BEPLAN Design + Build was commissioned by BZ WBK Arka Fund to deliver the complete fit-out of mBank’s MCO offices within the newly developed Park Business Teofilów (PBT) office complex in Łódź, Poland."},{"type":"p","text":"Covering approximately 4,000 m² across five floors, the project involved the comprehensive execution of architectural, construction, mechanical, electrical, and technical installations, transforming the newly developed office space into a fully operational corporate workplace."},{"type":"p","text":"The scope included open-plan workspaces, individual offices, conference and meeting rooms, collaborative areas, employee breakout spaces, circulation zones, and a fully equipped staff canteen."},{"type":"p","text":"A particularly important element of the project was the construction and technical integration of mBank’s main transaction server infrastructure, requiring dedicated electrical systems, mechanical installations, and close coordination of critical building services to meet the bank’s operational and security requirements."},{"type":"p","text":"The interior design combines functionality, efficiency, and employee comfort, featuring extensive glazed partitions, acoustic solutions, ergonomic workstations, contemporary finishes, and distinctive colour accents. The arrangement was developed to support both individual productivity and collaboration while maintaining a consistent corporate identity throughout the five floors."},{"type":"p","text":"As General Contractor, BEPLAN was responsible for coordinating and executing all construction activities, including architectural finishes, HVAC, electrical installations, lighting, structured cabling, technical infrastructure, and specialist subcontractors."},{"type":"p","text":"Despite the scale and technical complexity, the entire 4,000 m² project was successfully completed in approximately six months, demonstrating BEPLAN’s ability to deliver large-scale corporate fit-outs under demanding schedules and technical requirements."},{"type":"p","text":"Project execution and general contracting: BEPLAN Design + Build."}],"photos":6},"amundi":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"AMUNDI | Warsaw Headquarters | 1,000 m²"},{"type":"p","text":"BEPLAN Design + Build undertook the architectural and interior design of the Warsaw headquarters of Amundi, the internationally renowned French asset management company."},{"type":"p","text":"Located in Building 2 of Business Garden Warsaw, the 1,000 m² office was designed to reflect Amundi’s corporate identity through a modern, elegant, and functional architectural approach."},{"type":"p","text":"The project combines carefully planned workspaces, collaborative areas, welcoming lounges, integrated greenery, and contemporary materials. Special attention was given to space optimization, employee comfort, natural lighting, and architectural detailing, creating a sophisticated, efficient, and inspiring workplace."}],"photos":6},"zlota-44-residential-building":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Fitout of apartments floors 42 and 46."}],"photos":5},"bbc":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"BALMES BUSINESS CENTER – BARCELONA, SPAIN"},{"type":"p","text":"Office Refurbishment | Flexible Workspaces"},{"type":"p","text":"Located in a historic building on Barcelona’s prestigious Paseo de Gràcia, Balmes Business Center involved the refurbishment of an existing office into an elegant, flexible workspace offering part-time office rentals."},{"type":"p","text":"The project combines classical architectural character with contemporary functionality, featuring a welcoming reception, private offices, meeting rooms, and shared workspaces."},{"type":"p","text":"Original architectural details, decorative windows, natural wood flooring, warm lighting, and carefully selected finishes create a sophisticated professional environment that balances the building’s historical identity with the needs of a modern business center."}],"photos":6},"mbank-lb":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"mBank launched the project of light, ultra-modern banking outlets in shopping centres, equipped with touch screens with Kinect technology. It is a part of a complex project of redevelopment of the sales network scheduled for a few years, consisting in separating of redesigned branches and advisory centres from the current structure."},{"type":"p","text":"We executed the construction of 4 locations at the same time: Lodz, Szczecin, Gdynia and Gdansk."}],"photos":4},"mercedes-benz":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"1.500 sq.m Mercedes Benz latest state-of-the-art dealership. Contemporary in design and incorporating a cutting-edge service facility, waiting areas for clients and merchandise shop with the latest MB products."},{"type":"p","text":"Services:"},{"type":"li","text":"Execution design."},{"type":"li","text":"Project management."}],"photos":6},"ernst-young":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"We made a proposal for the complete refurbishment of EY’s reception area in RONDO 1 building, in Warsaw."}],"photos":6},"restaurant-el-madrono-terminal-4-madrid":{"blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"EL MADROÑO RESTAURANT | MADRID-BARAJAS AIRPORT, TERMINAL 4"},{"type":"p","text":"Located in Terminal 4 of Madrid-Barajas Airport, El Madroño Restaurant combines contemporary interior design with a refined and welcoming dining atmosphere."},{"type":"p","text":"The project integrates elegant dining areas, intimate private seating, and panoramic views of the airport terminal. Warm natural wood finishes, glass partitions, sophisticated lighting, and carefully selected furnishings create a harmonious balance between comfort, functionality, and architectural character."},{"type":"p","text":"Distinctive design elements include sculptural lighting features, curved architectural details, rich red upholstery, and bespoke furniture. The restaurant’s layout offers both open dining spaces overlooking the terminal and more intimate areas, creating a premium hospitality experience within the dynamic airport environment."}],"photos":6},"residence-konstancin-jeziorna-poland":{"blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"PRIVATE RESIDENCE | KONSTANCIN-JEZIORNA, POLAND"},{"type":"p","text":"This private residence in Konstancin-Jeziorna combines contemporary comfort with timeless elegance and a warm, natural character. The interior design features exposed wooden ceilings, natural timber flooring, custom-made furniture, and carefully integrated architectural lighting, creating a harmonious and welcoming living environment."},{"type":"p","text":"The project includes spacious living and dining areas, a functional kitchen, comfortable bedrooms, and elegant bathrooms. Large windows establish a strong connection between the interiors and the surrounding garden, bringing natural light into the living spaces."},{"type":"p","text":"A refined combination of natural materials, warm colours, decorative artwork, and carefully selected furnishings creates a sophisticated yet relaxed atmosphere, balancing functionality, comfort, and individual character."}],"photos":6},"max-sylt-brewery-barcelona":{"blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"MAX SYLT | BARCELONA, SPAIN"},{"type":"p","text":"Max Sylt is a contemporary bar-restaurant in Barcelona, combining industrial design with a warm and welcoming atmosphere. The interior features natural wood, exposed copper beer pipes, dark ceilings, and vibrant yellow accents that create a distinctive visual identity. A prominent central bar, custom furniture, and carefully integrated lighting bring together functionality, comfort, and character, creating a lively space for casual dining and social interaction."},{"type":"p","text":"I participated in the interior design in collaboration with renowned Barcelona-based designer Estrella Salietti, contributing to the creation of a sophisticated and functional hospitality environment."}],"photos":6},"rabat-jewelry-barcelona":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"RABAT JEWELLERY | BARCELONA, SPAIN"},{"type":"p","text":"The interior design of RABAT Jewellery reflects the elegance, exclusivity, and sophistication of luxury retail. The concept combines refined materials, carefully designed jewellery displays, elegant lighting, and a contemporary architectural language to create an intimate and welcoming shopping environment."},{"type":"p","text":"Special attention is given to showcasing fine jewellery and luxury watches, balancing aesthetics, functionality, and the customer experience."},{"type":"p","text":"I participated in the interior design in collaboration with renowned Barcelona-based designer Estrella Salietti, contributing to the creation of a sophisticated and functional hospitality environment."}],"photos":6},"polski-semon-gourmet-malaga-spain":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"SEMON | MÁLAGA, SPAIN"},{"type":"p","text":"Founded in Barcelona in 1962, Semon is a prestigious gourmet food, restaurant, and catering brand that expanded its presence to Madrid and Málaga. The interior design draws inspiration from natural bamboo textures, warm summer colours, and the relaxed Mediterranean beach atmosphere, creating a fresh, welcoming, and elegant space that reflects the essence of coastal living."},{"type":"p","text":"I participated in the interior design in collaboration with renowned Barcelona-based designer Estrella Salietti, contributing to the creation of a sophisticated and functional hospitality environment."}],"photos":6},"tuset":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Restaurant opened in Barcelona´s fashionable district of Eixample, and was considered a welcome addition to the thriving restaurant industry."},{"type":"p","text":"We decided to create an interior were people could be having lunch or dinner within the kitchen . We created no boundaries between kitchen and dining rooms. The fully opened kitchen allows diners to appreciate the preparation of food and the ability of cooks. The low hanging LED pendant lamps add a sparkling gleam above each table, attracting customers with a warm golden glow. Huge wine cellars store over 2,000 bottles of the best Spanish and international wines."},{"type":"p","text":"I participated in the interior design in collaboration with renowned Barcelona-based designer Estrella Salietti, contributing to the creation of a sophisticated and functional hospitality environment."}],"photos":6},"restaurant-museu-olympic":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Beplan was commissioned the project management and construction of the restaurant."},{"type":"p","text":"The restaurant area does not look out onto the street. One of its windowed sides balconies onto a room of the museum. All the services (bar, kitchen and bathrooms) are organized on the opposite side of the windows. The bell shaped lights, painted black on the outside, blend with the acoustic suspended ceiling, which is also black, while their bronze, silver and gold leaf interiors represent the history of the Olympic medal table."}],"photos":6},"vinyarroel":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"1.200sqm restaurant and winery located in Barcelona."},{"type":"p","text":"One of the most eye catching restaurant venues, boasting uniquely designed dining areas. Features a huge glass wine cellar in the heart of the restaurant, which contains more than 1.000 wine brands. A wooden stripe creates the feeling of dining under wooden barrels."}],"photos":6},"restaurant-romeo-juliet":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The project covers 650sq.m divided in 2 levels. This restaurant was designed for young clientele."},{"type":"p","text":"Epoxy floors, inscriptions on the ceilings, and minimalistic lines, create a subtle and elegant space. The design, balances opportunities to see and to be seen with intimate relaxing spaces."}],"photos":6},"iradier-house":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A single-family home located in the upper region of Barcelona, with views over the city."},{"type":"p","text":"The home is sited on the upper part of the section as a visual protection measure, while still allowing space for vehicle and pedestrian entrances. It is closed, via a brick and wooden latticework facade, from the two adjacent streets. The main façade, facing south with garden views, was built with large wooden and glass windows, combined with solid wood volumes. Solar protection is achieved through large, overhanging projections."}],"photos":6},"penthouse-passeig-de-gracia":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A new 800sq.m penthouse, with captivating views across Paseo de Gracia, Barcelona."},{"type":"p","text":"Injecting the house with a monochromatic palette made of stucco and mahogany wood resulted in an innovative and inspiring place to live. Doors covered in leather, white Thassos marble in the main bathroom, and a fully equipped Bulthaup kitchen, made this house one of the most slickest and sophisticated residences in Barcelona."}],"photos":6},"house-n":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"1500sq.m family house situated in Konstancin Jeziorna."},{"type":"p","text":"The residence has a certain European refinement mixed with American style. On the ground floor a central hallway provide access to the dining room, kitchen, and living room. A pair of open staircases lead to the home’s bridge and to 4 bedrooms, including the master suite. In these private quarters we integrated a tapestry of rich materials and textures: marble, brass, onyx, lacquer, bronze, silk, wool, and mirrored glass, which give color and texture that convey a deep sense of warmth."},{"type":"p","text":"Services:"},{"type":"li","text":"Executive project."},{"type":"li","text":"Project management."}],"photos":6},"kolorowe-osiedle":{"blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Modern architecture, eco-friendly materials, wide open spaces, green areas."},{"type":"p","text":"The location of the project is quiet and secluded, but well communicated with the city center. In close proximity there are shopping centers and leisure facilities. On the first stage two four level buildings were under construction, equipped with all necessary amenities. This phase includes 110 apartments, which were completed in April 2011. The total investment will accommodate 400 apartments."}],"photos":6}};
